**Verdict: accepted with P3** — P0: 0, P1: 0, P2: 0. One P3 remains.

- **P3 — `RE_REQUIRE_LAB` treats any set value as enabled.** The contract says `RE_REQUIRE_LAB=1`; the code checks only whether the variable exists, so `RE_REQUIRE_LAB=0` or an empty value also fails when the lab fixture is missing ([fixtures.rs](/home/sanya/orca/project/rust/crates/discord-conformance/tests/fixtures.rs:19)). This is a minor mismatch; the documented `=1` case works.
- **Retracted the manifest-path finding.** `realpath` resolves to `/home/sanya/orca/project/fixtures/MANIFEST.json`; the library builds that path from `fixtures_root()`, and the test asserts it ([lib.rs](/home/sanya/orca/project/rust/crates/discord-conformance/src/lib.rs:128), [fixtures.rs](/home/sanya/orca/project/rust/crates/discord-conformance/tests/fixtures.rs:35)).
- The lab-required red/green logs show the missing fixture fails and the present fixture passes. The ordinary path still returns success after printing `skip`; that remains a `cargo test` limitation under the repo’s “Skip ≠ pass” rule ([PROCESS.md](/home/sanya/orca/project/PROCESS.md:26), [fixtures.rs](/home/sanya/orca/project/rust/crates/discord-conformance/tests/fixtures.rs:26)). Treat the required-lab run as the acceptance check.
- `LEGAL.md` now marks keyring, log scanning, IP/payload redaction, and dependency license automation as incomplete or backlog items ([LEGAL.md](/home/sanya/orca/project/docs/rust-client/LEGAL.md:25), [LEGAL.md](/home/sanya/orca/project/docs/rust-client/LEGAL.md:45), [LEGAL.md](/home/sanya/orca/project/docs/rust-client/LEGAL.md:57), [LEGAL.md](/home/sanya/orca/project/docs/rust-client/LEGAL.md:75)).
